From 75370956265bf8de75af60fa79436171c5f4b0e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sam <sam@local>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:02:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cli): chat mode + agent/plan with selectable text tool
 mode

- new "chat" permission mode (Shift+Tab cycle, --mode chat): plain
  conversation, no tools offered (getRequestTools returns []), dedicated
  conversational system message without tool/commit contexts
- new tool mode "text": tools are described in the system message and
  tool calls are parsed from fenced ```tool code blocks in the reply -
  the native tools parameter is never sent, for OpenAI-compatible servers
  with unreliable function calling. Independent of the permission mode,
  works in agent (normal) and plan
- runtime selection in the interface: /tool-mode [native|text] slash
  command (toggles when no argument), mode indicator shows "tools:text"
- startup flags: --tool-mode native|text and --mode chat|normal|plan|auto
  (threaded through processCommandFlags -> initializeServices ->
  ToolPermissionService)
- switchToolMode on ToolPermissionService; text protocol implemented in
  tools/textToolMode.ts with unit tests (single/multiple fences, json
  fences tolerated, unknown tools and non-JSON blocks ignored, string
  arguments normalized)
---
